    "anatomicalJudgement": [
      "A regional peri-IMA display joins the actual source left-colic and connected sigmoid arterial neighborhoods, with separately authored neural continuations toward two independently confirmed external bowel-wall sites.",
      "The upper entry belongs to a medial descending-colonic arterial territory and the lower entry to a sigmoid-arterial turning region. The whole compound target remains intact; these observations do not define an exact descending/sigmoid boundary.",
      "The new structures represent a sympathetic contribution. Pelvic parasympathetic and upstream lumbar splanchnic/ganglion routes are not reconstructed or implied.",
      "The actual source-based departure sites are along represented artery courses, not recovered source arterial terminals. The illustrative neural departures do not extend or deform any source vessel."
    ],
    "limitations": [
      "Authored educational illustration, not measured nerve segmentation, clinical registration or complete innervation.",
      "Sparse representative threads, thickness, local junctions and exact wall approaches are authored. No histological plexus, intramural branch or actual nerve termination is claimed.",
      "The IMA regional display begins distal to the original aortic interface conflict, while retaining both represented colonic branching neighborhoods.",
      "Positive terminal clearances describe actual exported vertex/cap samples, not a continuous triangle-to-triangle global minimum. No physical wall contact is claimed.",
      "Original arterial mouths remain open; projected original boundary portals are auxiliary tests, not added source caps. Per-component normals, strict triangle crossings and local oriented brackets complement them.",
      "Source-section containment can need interpretation around joined end rims; complementary actual ray intervals and local outer-wall probes are retained. Rays with no source hit are unclassified by that ray alone.",
      "The original source anatomy and accepted 4747/6988 nerve assets remain unchanged. No exact canonical nerve aliases or artificial target subdivisions are introduced."
    ],
